{% doc %}
  Formats a price the same way `| money` does, except for EUR (the Slovenian
  market), where the client wants the € symbol placed after the amount instead
  of before it (e.g. "19,99 €" instead of "€19,99").

  This can't be solved in the Shopify admin: Settings > General > Change
  currency formatting only applies to the store's own currency (USD). The
  format of other currencies sold through Markets (like EUR) is fixed by
  Shopify and has no setting. So the EUR-only placement is handled here
  instead, and every other currency keeps using Shopify's formatting untouched.
  The JS side (prices updated after a variant change or cart update) gets the
  same treatment through `theme.moneyFormat` in snippets/js-bridge.liquid.

  Use this snippet instead of the `money` filters anywhere a price is shown.

  @param {number} amount - A price in the currency's smallest unit (cents), e.g. variant.price
  @param {boolean} [with_currency] - Also show the currency code, like money_with_currency
  @param {boolean} [trim_zeros] - Drop a trailing .00, like money_without_trailing_zeros. Ignored for EUR, which always shows 2 decimals (standard for it).
  @param {string} [currency] - ISO code of the amount's currency, when it isn't the current one (e.g. order.currency). Defaults to the visitor's current currency.

  @example
  {% render 'money', amount: variant.price %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign currency_code = currency.iso_code | default: currency | default: cart.currency.iso_code
-%}
{%- if currency_code == 'EUR' -%}
  {{- amount | money_without_currency -}}&nbsp;€
{%- elsif with_currency -%}
  {{- amount | money_with_currency -}}
{%- elsif trim_zeros -%}
  {{- amount | money_without_trailing_zeros -}}
{%- else -%}
  {{- amount | money -}}
{%- endif -%}